Author: blackdream1234 <12joseph.jh@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Jul 24 13:51:27 2026 +0300

    Cache tree/domain-invariant facts in weak-AXp checking
    
    extract_axp_deletion / extract_final_tree_axps call weak_axp_check once
    per feature-deletion trial and once per held-out row, and each call
    recomputed backend_meta (a function of the tree only) and is_binary_domain
    (a full O(rows x features) rescan of the reference domain, invariant across
    the whole extraction) from scratch. Profiling on letter.dl8 (224 features,
    depth-5 tree) showed this rescan alone was 99.8% of AXp-extraction time
    versus 0.1% for the actual certified GF(2)/Horn/AntiHorn/2-SAT solve, and
    the strict full-corpus benchmark was on track for ~20 days.
    
    Hoist both into an AxpCheckContext computed once per tree/domain pair and
    threaded through *_with_context variants. weak_axp_check and
    extract_axp_deletion keep identical public signatures and behavior (they
    build the context internally); only repeat callers reuse it.
    
    This is a correctness-neutral change: the cached bool is the exact value
    the old code recomputed every call, so every certification decision, AXp,
    and reported metric is unchanged. Verified by:
    - 7 new equivalence unit tests (cached vs uncached path, byte-identical
      WeakAxpResult / AxpResult across certified success, non-Boolean-domain
      rejection, dimension-mismatch, out-of-bounds row, and empirical mode);
    - the full existing suite (161 -> 168 tests, all pass unchanged);
    - an end-to-end A/B benchmark (3 datasets x 8 methods, before-fix vs
      after-fix binary): 0 differences across all 88 non-timing columns
      (accuracy, tree structure, theorem_certified, backend, path state,
      axp_valid_rate, axp_minimal_rate, pruning/search diagnostics), with the
      only residual variance (predicate_mask_cache_hits/misses) shown to be
      pre-existing run-to-run noise present between two runs of the same binary;
    - a direct measurement: 112.26s -> 0.062s for 30 rows of letter.dl8,
      same certification result (valid=30, minimal=30).

